# D19 decision (Astra for the orchestrator, 2026-10-17): tests/test_capacity_holds.py, tests/test_capacity_pool.py, tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py

Decision: LAND

- `tests/test_capacity_holds.py`: The empty-PGID case now expects release and zero charged slots, while additionally preserving the custody fence (`tests/test_capacity_holds.py:170`). This is the row’s explicit reversal, implemented at `src/otto/portfolio/execution_host.py:820`. The surviving-member test still requires a held slot (`tests/test_capacity_holds.py:185`), so premature release remains detectable.

- `tests/test_capacity_pool.py`: Previously silent pin failures now require exceptions while retaining the no-record checks (`tests/test_capacity_pool.py:443`, `tests/test_capacity_pool.py:450`, `tests/test_capacity_pool.py:453`, `tests/test_capacity_pool.py:528`). These expectations enforce the required launch gate implemented at `src/otto/agents/owner_runtime.py:50`; swallowed failures would fail them. Profiling replaces the product-method patch and preserves the exact owner-thread registration assertion (`tests/test_capacity_pool.py:487`, `tests/test_capacity_pool.py:508`), which still fails if registration disappears or moves to the transport thread.

- `tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py`: Successful admission now runs through the real owner while preserving success, tools, session binding, observer cleanup and replay checks (`tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:196`). An already-exited initializer now requires a specific registration failure, completed/failed Due and no hold (`tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:412`), matching mandatory registration before input (`src/otto/agents/claude_cli.py:381`). Direct transport exit diagnostics remain protected (`tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:398`). Added durable-initializer checks and real filesystem failure injection strengthen protection against missing pins, surviving groups, input delivery and retained slots (`tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:151`, `tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:262`, `tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:306`, `tests/test_claude_manager_admission.py:323`). They use independent process, disk and retained-state evidence without patching product methods or adding timer-based success conditions.